## Google Live endpoint and exact Markdown source preservation — 2026-11-16

- CI run #2028 (`43817339513`) still failed the two Markdown source-preservation tests. The indentation-prefix workaround did not solve the formatter's whitespace transformation. Replaced the Chroma terminal formatter with a small native-Go ANSI emitter: Chroma still performs grammar tokenization and Monokai style lookup, while original token values are emitted unchanged. Tabs, indentation, CRLF/newline bytes and source ordering are not normalized; ANSI sequences are inserted only around styled token text.
- Google Cloud's current Gemini Live Agent Platform guide specifies `/ws/google.cloud.aiplatform.v1.LlmBidiService/BidiGenerateContent` and the regional host `{LOCATION}-aiplatform.googleapis.com`. The existing ADC implementation used the obsolete `v1beta1` service path and omitted the location prefix when `LOCATION=global`; both prevent the documented endpoint from matching. Updated the default endpoint builder and tests for `us-central1`, `global`, and the exact v1 path.
- Updated README credential documentation to distinguish the routes: Gemini Developer API and AI Studio remain shared-API-key providers; Gemini Live supports either the Developer API key path or Agent Platform ADC. The ADC instructions now name `gcloud auth application-default login`, `GOOGLE_CLOUD_PROJECT`, `GOOGLE_CLOUD_LOCATION`, and the required Vertex AI project access.
- Ctrl+L regression test and the event trace / Markdown renderer implementation remain in place. The next CI run must confirm all package tests, vet and the static Linux build; no live Google account credentials are available in CI, so ADC validation is covered by an injected-token WebSocket handshake test rather than a production-account call.


- CI run #2029 (`43818219625`) and #2030 (`43818332713`) both reached `go test ./...` but failed the same two tab-preservation assertions. Replacing the terminal formatter was insufficient because Chroma's lexer itself expands literal tabs before yielding token values. The final fix now substitutes tabs with one-byte spaces before lexing, validates the emitted token stream byte-for-byte against that placeholder source, and restores the original tab bytes at the matching source offsets. If Chroma ever changes token text or token coverage, highlighting falls back to the untouched original source rather than altering content.
- Corrected the Agent Platform ADC test fixture to use the same v1 path constant as the production endpoint builder.


- CI run #2031 (`43818818025`) confirmed the two Markdown tab assertions still failed after Chroma input substitution. Root cause found in `internal/tui/terminal_text.go`: `sanitizeTerminalText(text, false)` intentionally expands every tab to four spaces. The Markdown renderer called this sanitizer before tokenization, making it impossible for downstream highlighting to recover the original source.
- Added a Markdown-specific safe sanitizer that preserves literal tabs and line boundaries while still replacing ESC and dropping other terminal control bytes. Both full-message rendering and streamed chunks now use it. The generic terminal-output sanitizer remains unchanged for other TUI surfaces.


